    { math: '1 · Agenda-setting', note: 'Why do SOME problems reach government? Attention is scarce (Kingdon\'s "policy windows"): a problem gets noticed, a solution exists waiting, and politics opens a window — streams align or nothing happens.' },
    { math: '2 · Formulation and adoption', note: 'Options are drafted (by civil servants, think tanks, lobbyists) and chosen — through bargaining, coalitions and veto points. The US system has many veto points; the UK system few — the same problem yields different policies.' },
